<title>JAPAN: Japan August nickel imports tumble 33.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan August nickel imports tumble 33.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports totalled 3,627 tonnes in August, off 33.6 percent from 5,465 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		 August 96     July 96     August 95</p>
<p> Total	   3,627	  4,194	 5,465</p>
<p>Major suppliers:  Russia	    601	    770	 2,089</p>
<p> S. Africa	 265	    350	   380</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  354	    520	   501</p>
<p>Imports in the first eight months of 1996 totalled 37,687 tonnes, against 48,817 tonnes in the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
